MCP Student Management System

A Student Management System built using Model Context Protocol (MCP), FastMCP, Python, SQLite, and Google Gemini.

This project allows an AI assistant to interact with a student database through MCP tools. The user can communicate with the system using natural language, and Google Gemini can select the appropriate MCP tool to perform operations such as creating, updating, deleting, searching, analyzing, and managing student records.

Project Overview

The main purpose of this project is to understand how Model Context Protocol (MCP) can connect an AI model with external tools and data.

In this project:

Google Gemini acts as the AI layer.

MCP Client communicates with the MCP Server.

FastMCP Server provides tools for student management.

Database Layer handles SQLite operations.

SQLite stores student information.

The user does not need to directly write SQL queries. Instead, the user can ask questions in natural language.

Example:

Show me the marks of Rahul.

Gemini understands the request and selects the appropriate MCP tool.

