Complete Request Flow

User
  ↓
Natural Language Request
  ↓
Google Gemini
  ↓
Select Appropriate MCP Tool
  ↓
MCP Client
  ↓
MCP Server
  ↓
Database Layer
  ↓
SQLite Database
  ↓
Result
  ↓
MCP Client
  ↓
Google Gemini
  ↓
Final Response

How the System Works

The user sends a request in natural language.

Google Gemini understands the user's request.

Gemini determines which MCP tool is required.

The MCP Client sends the tool request to the MCP Server.

The MCP Server executes the appropriate operation.

The database layer communicates with SQLite.

The result is returned through the MCP Server and MCP Client.

Gemini generates the final natural-language response.

Example

User:

What are Rahul's marks?

System flow:

User
  ↓
Gemini understands the request
  ↓
Gemini selects an appropriate MCP tool
  ↓
MCP Client calls MCP Server
  ↓
MCP Server accesses database.py
  ↓
SQLite database is queried
  ↓
Rahul's marks are returned
  ↓
Gemini generates final answer
  ↓
User receives the answer

