Database

The project uses SQLite to store student information.

Student records contain information such as:

Student ID
Student Name
Course
Marks
Attendance

Example:

Student ID: 102
Name: Rahul
Course: Computer
Marks: 78
Attendance: 85%

The database.py file provides functions for creating, reading, updating, deleting, searching, and analyzing student records.

Database Architecture

MCP Tool
   ↓
server.py
   ↓
database.py
   ↓
SQLite Connection
   ↓
students.db

The database logic is kept separately from the MCP server logic.

This separation makes the project easier to maintain, debug, and extend.

CRUD Operations

The project supports complete CRUD operations.

CRUD means:

C → Create
R → Read
U → Update
D → Delete

Create

Create a new student:

Create student 107 named Amit in Mechanical with marks 85 and attendance 90.

Read

Retrieve student information:

Show me student 102.

Update

Update student information:

Update Rahul's marks to 90.

Delete

Delete a student:

Delete student 107.

