Example Complete Workflow

Suppose the user asks:

Analyze student 102.

The complete flow is:

1. User sends request
        ↓
2. Gemini understands the request
        ↓
3. Gemini identifies the required MCP tool
        ↓
4. MCP Client calls the MCP Server
        ↓
5. MCP Server executes the tool
        ↓
6. Tool accesses database.py
        ↓
7. database.py reads students.db
        ↓
8. Student information is returned
        ↓
9. MCP Client sends the result to Gemini
        ↓
10. Gemini generates the final response
        ↓
11. User receives the answer

Why MCP?

Traditional AI applications often need custom integrations for every external tool or data source.

MCP provides a standardized way for an AI application to communicate with external tools and data.

In this project:

Gemini = AI / Reasoning Layer

MCP Client = Communication Layer

MCP Server = Tool Layer

database.py = Database Access Layer

SQLite = Data Storage Layer

This separation makes the system modular and easier to extend.

Advantages of This Architecture

Natural-language interaction

AI-powered tool selection

Standardized MCP communication

Modular design

Separate database layer

SQLite database integration

CRUD operations

Bulk data insertion

Student search

Marks analysis

Attendance analysis

Student comparison

Student ranking

Student reports

Dynamic tool discovery

